                              "disease_code":  "ERECTILE_DYSFUNCTION_FOLLOWING_SIMPLE_PROSTATECTOMY",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Erectile dysfunction following radical prostatectomy follows removal of the prostate and surrounding tissue for cancer (higher nerve-injury risk); following simple prostatectomy follows removal of prostate tissue for benign disease (e.g., BPH), with lower nerve-injury risk."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "ERECTILE_DYSFUNCTION_FOLLOWING_RADICAL_CYSTECTOMY",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Erectile dysfunction following radical prostatectomy follows prostate removal; following radical cystectomy follows bladder removal, which also risks the neurovascular bundles but via a different surgical field and indication (bladder cancer, not prostate cancer)."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "ERECTILE_DYSFUNCTION_FOLLOWING_URETHRAL_SURGERY",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Erectile dysfunction following radical prostatectomy is linked to pelvic nerve-sparing surgery for prostate cancer; following urethral surgery is linked to procedures on the urethra itself (e.g., stricture repair), a different anatomical mechanism of injury."
                          }
